  "segments": [
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0001",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 0.57,
      "end_seconds": 2.56,
      "duration_seconds": 1.99,
      "text": "morning, come on through"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0002",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 4.65,
      "end_seconds": 8.14,
      "duration_seconds": 3.49,
      "text": "morning, doctor, sorry about the rush"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0003",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 8.64,
      "end_seconds": 11.22,
      "duration_seconds": 2.58,
      "text": "how are things, what's been happening?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0004",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 12.48,
      "end_seconds": 18.96,
      "duration_seconds": 6.48,
      "text": "Ah, doctor, it's spots on my face. It's getting on my nerves now."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0005",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 23.73,
      "end_seconds": 28.63,
      "duration_seconds": 4.9,
      "text": "Since when exactly? It helps to to be thorough at this stage."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0006",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 30.0,
      "end_seconds": 32.96,
      "duration_seconds": 2.96,
      "text": "I've had it for two years."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0007",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 34.93,
      "end_seconds": 37.92,
      "duration_seconds": 2.99,
      "text": "How much trouble does it give you?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0008",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 39.69,
      "end_seconds": 41.54,
      "duration_seconds": 1.85,
      "text": "I'd call it moderate."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0009",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 43.58,
      "end_seconds": 47.49,
      "duration_seconds": 3.91,
      "text": "what about sore red lumps, have you noticed that?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0010",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 48.98,
      "end_seconds": 58.99,
      "duration_seconds": 10.01,
      "text": "Yeah. Three weeks, I'd say. I did have spots on my back at one point, but that's gone now."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0011",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "NURSE",
      "start_seconds": 60.41,
      "end_seconds": 70.59,
      "duration_seconds": 10.18,
      "text": "okay, so the vitals from earlier. Temperature 36.5, respiratory rate 18, blood pressure 109 over 74, saturation 99 percent, pulse is 71 beats a minute"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0012",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 72.43,
      "end_seconds": 74.42,
      "duration_seconds": 1.99,
      "text": "So, good, thank you."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0013",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 76.69,
      "end_seconds": 79.02,
      "duration_seconds": 2.33,
      "text": "May I examine you now?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0014",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 80.01,
      "end_seconds": 83.4,
      "duration_seconds": 3.39,
      "text": "So, I'll listen to your chest now."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0015",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 93.44,
      "end_seconds": 101.51,
      "duration_seconds": 8.07,
      "text": "there are red inflamed lumps and blackheads over both cheeks and the forehead, and a few scars"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0016",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 106.29,
      "end_seconds": 113.8,
      "duration_seconds": 7.51,
      "text": "You can sit up now. A few quick ones: being pregnant, fever or joint pain?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0017",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 114.49,
      "end_seconds": 117.23,
      "duration_seconds": 2.74,
      "text": "No, nothing to report there."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0018",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 119.31,
      "end_seconds": 120.26,
      "duration_seconds": 0.95,
      "text": "Any headaches?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0019",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 121.75,
      "end_seconds": 126.49,
      "duration_seconds": 4.74,
      "text": "Okay, so so not that I've noticed, no headaches."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0020",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 128.41,
      "end_seconds": 130.65,
      "duration_seconds": 2.24,
      "text": "Is your digestion otherwise okay?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0021",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 131.25,
      "end_seconds": 133.6,
      "duration_seconds": 2.35,
      "text": "bowels are regular, nothing odd"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0022",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 135.38,
      "end_seconds": 137.93,
      "duration_seconds": 2.55,
      "text": "Is your urine normal, no changes?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0023",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 138.5,
      "end_seconds": 139.88,
      "duration_seconds": 1.38,
      "text": "No changes there."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0024",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 141.79,
      "end_seconds": 145.35,
      "duration_seconds": 3.56,
      "text": "Tell me about any past illnesses or ongoing conditions."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0025",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 147.41,
      "end_seconds": 149.02,
      "duration_seconds": 1.61,
      "text": "I've got anxiety"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0026",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 150.36,
      "end_seconds": 153.23,
      "duration_seconds": 2.87,
      "text": "now some background about your lifestyle"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0027",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 155.14,
      "end_seconds": 173.82,
      "duration_seconds": 18.68,
      "text": "I smoke roughly a pack every two days. I only drink at family occasions. I walk the dog every morning. I live with my elderly mother. Lots of rice, lentils and some fruit."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0028",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 174.45,
      "end_seconds": 176.6,
      "duration_seconds": 2.15,
      "text": "Tell me your medicines, please."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0029",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 178.03,
      "end_seconds": 180.52,
      "duration_seconds": 2.49,
      "text": "Face wash, twice a day"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0030",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 181.6,
      "end_seconds": 184.97,
      "duration_seconds": 3.37,
      "text": "How long have you been on it?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0031",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 186.45,
      "end_seconds": 193.75,
      "duration_seconds": 7.3,
      "text": "About about a month. I had escitalopram at one point, but I'm off it now."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0032",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 208.24,
      "end_seconds": 211.38,
      "duration_seconds": 3.14,
      "text": "Has anyone in your family had anything serious?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0033",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 212.4,
      "end_seconds": 214.38,
      "duration_seconds": 1.98,
      "text": "my brother has epilepsy"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0034",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 228.74,
      "end_seconds": 231.45,
      "duration_seconds": 2.71,
      "text": "Have you had any previous surgeries?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0035",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 232.45,
      "end_seconds": 235.57,
      "duration_seconds": 3.12,
      "text": "No, I've never been operated on."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0036",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 246.93,
      "end_seconds": 251.79,
      "duration_seconds": 4.86,
      "text": "are you allergic to anything? Any allergies to medicines or foods?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0037",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 253.42,
      "end_seconds": 257.43,
      "duration_seconds": 4.01,
      "text": "Erm, not to to my knowledge, no."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0038",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 258.26,
      "end_seconds": 267.41,
      "duration_seconds": 9.15,
      "text": "So, based on the history and the examination, I'd lean towards moderate inflammatory acne. I'd also keep a hormonal cause in mind."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0039",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 268.53,
      "end_seconds": 271.96,
      "duration_seconds": 3.43,
      "text": "I'm scared it's something bad. Is it?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0040",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 272.5,
      "end_seconds": 310.69,
      "duration_seconds": 38.19,
      "text": "I can't promise yet, but most people with moderate inflammatory acne do well once it's treated properly. Blood tests is what I'd like next, for acne treatment baseline. I'd like you to take adapalene gel, 0.1 percent, once a night, for twelve weeks. That should help with acne. Use sunscreen daily, and the gel can sting for the first couple of weeks. I'll also refer you to the dermatology clinic. Book a review in twelve weeks."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0041",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 312.64,
      "end_seconds": 316.58,
      "duration_seconds": 3.94,
      "text": "Alright, anything else on your mind before you go?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0042",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 317.19,
      "end_seconds": 320.4,
      "duration_seconds": 3.21,
      "text": "No, that's all. Thanks a lot."
    }
  ]
}